{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Sacrifice</b> — The reason for mentioning all this is that the offerings I commanded you to bring before Me do not benefit Me, only you." "And the meaning of <b>thanksgiving</b> — for the burnt offering is entirely offered up, while the sin-offering and the guilt-offering belong to the priest. And the meaning is: to offer a thanksgiving offering along with observance of the Torah, since from it no offerings go up to the Most High except those so specified, is better than a burnt offering without thanksgiving."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:26.852430487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}